  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana has $1.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Montana has 8,264 awards with an average award size of $161K, and obligations are up 15.9% year over year. Montana moved from $691M in FY21, to $925M in FY22, then to $1B in FY23, and to $1.1B in both FY24 and FY25 before reaching $1.3B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Montana and obligated $419M so far. The Department of Agriculture follows with $356M and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $190M. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC is the largest vendor with $135M in obligations, followed by BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC with $80.6M and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV with $58.9M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest industry by obligations with $198M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $155M and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance with $137M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Montana federal obligations over recent years?",
        "body": "Montana’s obligations rose from $691M in FY21 to $925M in FY22, then to $1B in FY23 and $1.1B in FY24 and FY25, before reaching $1.3B in FY26. Montana’s obligations are up 15.9% year over year for FY2026 to date. Montana’s average award size across those obligations is $161K. The total award count for FY2026 to date is 8,264."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate the FY2026 to date picture?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $419M, then the Department of Agriculture with $356M and the Department of Homeland Security with $190M. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC is the top vendor with $135M, followed by BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC with $80.6M and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV with $58.9M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation has $198M in obligations, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction has $155M, and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance has $137M."
      }
    ]
